  "rule": "Rhythm rule 2, fixed before it was run. R1c = R1 with the log-interval deviations re-centred over the beats that fall inside the 30 s window (DURATION + one mean interval), so the in-window mean rate equals the command. Real windows: test split of the six original datasets and the three PTT contexts, otherwise as RULE_RHYTHM (same features, score and seed). R1c replaces R0 if its overall score is lower than R0's by more than 20% and its mean absolute error of the mean rate is <= 1 bpm. Guard, relative: for each deployed generator (PhysioMix, PhysioFlow), on up to 24 test windows per original dataset, the mean absolute error between the strip's detected rate (flow.window_peaks) and the command with R1c encoded into z must not exceed the same error with R0 encoded by more than 0.5 bpm.",
